      "content": "I do not have real-time, specific local data to cite definitive studies for you right now, but the \"benefit cliff\" is a well-discussed concept in labor economics. This issue, where a small increase in earned income can lead to a large loss of benefits, is frequently the focus of policy research and it is often shown in targeted impact studies. You should look for recent government or think-tank analyses specifically focusing on the \"marginal tax and benefit rate\" to see the empirical evidence for this disincentive.",
